<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Idle/Incremental Game Market Analysis</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
           margin: 0; background: #f8f9fa; color: #212529; }
    header { background: #1a1a2e; color: #eee; padding: 2rem 2rem 1.5rem; }
    header h1 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 1.8rem; }
    header p  { margin: 0; opacity: 0.75; font-size: 0.95rem; }
    nav { background: #16213e; padding: 0.5rem 2rem; }
    nav a { color: #aac4ff; text-decoration: none; margin-right: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    nav a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
    main { max-width: 1200px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem 4rem; }
    section { background: #fff; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
              margin-bottom: 2rem; box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.08); }
    h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin-top: 0; border-bottom: 2px solid #e9ecef; padding-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; color: #495057; }
    .caption { font-size: 0.82rem; color: #6c757d; margin: 0.3rem 0 1rem;
               border-left: 3px solid #dee2e6; padding-left: 0.6rem; }
    .honesty { background: #fff3cd; border: 1px solid #ffc107; border-radius: 4px;
               padding: 0.6rem 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #664d03; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .stat-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .stat { background: #f1f3f5; border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; min-width: 140px; }
    .stat .val { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1a1a2e; }
    .stat .lbl { font-size: 0.78rem; color: #868e96; }
    ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
    li { margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
    .reddit-note { background: #e7f3ff; border-left: 4px solid #74b9ff;
                   padding: 0.7rem 1rem; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;
                   font-size: 0.88rem; color: #2d3436; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    footer { text-align: center; font-size: 0.78rem; color: #adb5bd;
             padding: 2rem 0 1rem; }
    .chart-wrap { margin: 1rem 0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <h1>Idle / Incremental Game Market Analysis</h1>
  <p>Steam catalogue analysis — data sourced from SteamSpy and Steam store pages.
     Owner counts are modeled estimates, not verified sales.
     Mobile not covered. See <a href="methodology.html" style="color:#aac4ff">Methodology</a> for full caveats.</p>
</header>
<nav>
  <a href="#themes">Themes</a>
  <a href="#gaps">Gaps</a>
  <a href="#performance">Performance</a>
  <a href="#features">Features</a>
  <a href="#monetization">Monetization</a>
  <a href="#art">Art Style</a>
  <a href="#updates">Updates</a>
  <a href="#trends">Trends</a>
  <a href="#naming">Naming</a>
  <a href="#supplementary">Supplementary</a>
  <a href="methodology.html">Methodology</a>
</nav>
<main>

  <!-- =========================================================
       EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
  ========================================================= -->
  <section id="summary">
    <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
    {% if dataset and dataset.total_games %}
    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="val">{{ dataset.total_games }}</div>
        <div class="lbl">Idle/incremental games analyzed</div>
      </div>
      {% if dataset.with_reviews %}
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="val">{{ dataset.with_reviews }}</div>
        <div class="lbl">With Steam review data</div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if dataset.themed %}
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="val">{{ dataset.themed }}</div>
        <div class="lbl">Classified into themes</div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    <p class="caption">Dataset generated {{ dataset.generated_utc }}.
      {{ dataset.with_reviews }} games have Steam review data;
      {{ dataset.themed }} classified into themes.</p>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="honesty">
      <strong>Data honesty:</strong> All figures come from the analysis JSON.
      Owner counts are SteamSpy estimates (modeled, not audited sales).
      Mobile is not covered. Reddit sentiment is
      {% if supp_reddit.available %}available (cached){% else %}unavailable (403/no OAuth){% endif %}.
    </div>

    <div class="stat-row">
      {% if n_themes %}
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="val">{{ n_themes }}</div>
        <div class="lbl">Themes identified</div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if supp_itch.count %}
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="val">{{ supp_itch.count }}</div>
        <div class="lbl">itch.io titles (one page)</div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if supp_kong.count %}
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="val">{{ supp_kong.count }}</div>
        <div class="lbl">Kongregate titles (one page)</div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    <p>
      This report analyses the idle/incremental game market using Steam as the
      quantitative spine{% if n_themes %}, finding <strong>{{ n_themes }} distinct themes</strong>{% endif %}.
      {% if top_theme and top_theme != '—' %}
      The most represented theme in the corpus is <strong>{{ top_theme }}</strong>
      (classified by description keyword matching — medium-low confidence; see Methodology).
      {% endif %}
      {% if top_perf_theme and top_perf_theme != '—' %}
      By weighted performance score (review % × log owners), <strong>{{ top_perf_theme }}</strong>
      leads the ranking.
      {% endif %}
      {% if underserved_themes %}
      Potentially underserved niches (low supply, high demand):
      <strong>{{ underserved_themes | join(", ") }}</strong>.
      {% endif %}
    </p>

    <h3>Building an Idler: What the Data Says</h3>
    <ul>
      {% if positive_features %}
      <li><strong>Features that correlate with higher reviews:</strong>
          {{ positive_features | join(", ") }}.
          (Correlation, not causation; n may be small — see quality chart.)</li>
      {% endif %}
      {% if rising_themes %}
      <li><strong>Rising themes</strong> (better recent-year reviews than older releases):
          {{ rising_themes | join(", ") }}.</li>
      {% endif %}
      <li>Update cadence matters: the update-cadence chart shows whether active
          upkeep correlates with review score in this corpus.</li>
      <li>Price and business model: the monetization charts show how free-to-play
          and paid tiers distribute across the catalogue.</li>
      <li><em>Mobile is not covered. The above reflects Steam only.</em></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- =========================================================
       THEMES
  ========================================================= -->
  <section id="themes">
    <h2>Theme Landscape</h2>
    <p class="caption">
      n = number of games per theme. Owner counts are SteamSpy modeled estimates —
      not verified sales. Weighted score = review% × log(1 + owners).
    </p>
    <div class="honesty">
      <strong>Theme caveat (medium-low confidence):</strong> Themes are classified
      by keyword word-boundary matching against each game's <em>short description</em>
      only — per-game Steam tags were not available from the data source used.
      This is a heuristic: a game may be mis-classified if its description contains
      thematic words incidentally. Treat theme counts as directional signals, not
      authoritative genre data. See <a href="methodology.html">Methodology</a> for details.
    </div>
    {% if figures.theme_bar %}
    <div class="chart-wrap">{{ figures.theme_bar | safe }}</div>
    {% else %}
    <p><em>No theme data available.</em></p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <!-- =========================================================
       GAPS
  ========================================================= -->
  <section id="gaps">
    <h2>Supply vs Demand Gap Map</h2>
    <p class="caption">
      Supply = number of games (Steam corpus). Demand = weighted score (review% × log owners,
      SteamSpy estimates). Red markers are underserved themes: supply ≤ 25th percentile
      AND demand ≥ median. Confidence: medium — thresholds sensitive to corpus size.
    </p>
    {% if figures.gap_scatter %}
    <div class="chart-wrap">{{ figures.gap_scatter | safe }}</div>
    {% else %}
    <p><em>No gap data available.</em></p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <!-- =========================================================
       PERFORMANCE
  ========================================================= -->
  <section id="performance">
    <h2>Theme Performance Ranking</h2>
    <p class="caption">
      Weighted score = review_pct_positive × log(1 + total_owners).
      Owner counts are SteamSpy estimates. Themes with no owner data excluded.
    </p>
    {% if figures.performance_bar %}
    <div class="chart-wrap">{{ figures.performance_bar | safe }}</div>
    {% else %}
    <p><em>No performance data available.</em></p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <!-- =========================================================
       FEATURES
  ========================================================= -->
  <section id="features">
    <h2>Feature Impact on Review Score</h2>
    <p class="caption">
      Delta = mean review % for games <em>with</em> the feature minus
      mean review % for games <em>without</em>. Positive = feature correlates
      with higher reviews. This is correlation only — small n may be unreliable.
      Features: offline_progress, prestige (mechanic tags), is_free (price field).
    </p>
    {% if figures.feature_delta %}
    <div class="chart-wrap">{{ figures.feature_delta | safe }}</div>
    {% else %}
    <p><em>No feature data available.</em></p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <!-- =========================================================
       MONETIZATION
  ========================================================= -->
  <section id="monetization">
    <h2>Monetization Analysis</h2>
    <p class="caption">
      Business model and price bucket breakdown. Owner counts are SteamSpy modeled
      estimates. Prices from Steam store pages at scrape time — may not reflect
      discounts or regional pricing.
    </p>
    {% if figures.monetization_bar %}
    <h3>Business Models</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap">{{ figures.monetization_bar | safe }}</div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if figures.price_buckets %}
    <h3>Price Buckets (USD)</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap">{{ figures.price_buckets | safe }}</div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if not figures.monetization_bar and not figures.price_buckets %}
    <p><em>No monetization data available.</em></p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <!-- =========================================================
       ART STYLE
  ========================================================= -->
  <section id="art">
    <h2>Art Style Distribution</h2>
    <p class="caption">
      Art style classification depended on per-game Steam tags, which were not
      available from the data source used in this pipeline. Art style is null
      for all 3,479 games — no art style chart can be rendered. This is a known
      pipeline limitation, not a rendering error. See
      <a href="methodology.html">Methodology</a> for details.
    </p>
    {% if figures.art_bar %}
    <div class="chart-wrap">{{ figures.art_bar | safe }}</div>
    {% else %}
    <p><em>Art style data unavailable — per-game Steam tags were not accessible via the SteamSpy endpoint used. Art style is null for all games in this dataset.</em></p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <!-- =========================================================
       UPDATES
  ========================================================= -->
  <section id="updates">
    <h2>Update Cadence</h2>
    <p class="caption">
      Active ≤ 30 days since last update; Occasional 31–120 days; Abandoned > 120 days
      or no update detected. Update dates from Steam store scrape.
    </p>
    {% if figures.update_cadence %}
    <div class="chart-wrap">{{ figures.update_cadence | safe }}</div>
    {% else %}
    <p><em>No update cadence data available.</em></p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <!-- =========================================================
       TRENDS
  ========================================================= -->
  <section id="trends">
    <h2>Release Trends</h2>
    <p class="caption">
      Releases per year from Steam release dates.
      {% if n_trends_years %}Covers {{ n_trends_years }} calendar years.{% endif %}
      Median review % per year shown on secondary axis.
    </p>
    {% if figures.releases_per_year %}
    <div class="chart-wrap">{{ figures.releases_per_year | safe }}</div>
    {% else %}
    <p><em>No trend data available.</em></p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <!-- =========================================================
       NAMING PATTERNS
  ========================================================= -->
  <section id="naming">
    <h2>Naming Patterns</h2>
    <p class="caption">
      Pattern counts and mean review % by title keyword match. Patterns are derived
      from game title keywords only (e.g. titles starting with "Idle …" = idle_x;
      titles ending in "… Clicker" = x_clicker; all others = creative). This is a
      surface-level heuristic — not a validated genre classification.
    </p>
    {% if figures.naming_bar %}
    <div class="chart-wrap">{{ figures.naming_bar | safe }}</div>
    {% else %}
    <p><em>No naming pattern data available.</em></p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <!-- =========================================================
       SUPPLEMENTARY SOURCES
  ========================================================= -->
  <section id="supplementary">
    <h2>Supplementary Sources</h2>
    <div class="honesty">
      Supplementary sources are informational only — they are <strong>not</strong>
      combined with Steam data in the charts above (different confidence levels and
      data shapes prevent honest cross-source comparison).
    </div>

    <h3>itch.io</h3>
    {% if supp_itch %}
    <ul>
      <li>Titles found (one browse page): <strong>{{ supp_itch.count | default('n/a') }}</strong></li>
      <li>Free titles: <strong>{{ supp_itch.free_count | default('n/a') }}</strong>
          ({{ supp_itch.free_pct | default('n/a') }}%)</li>
      {% if supp_itch.top_tags %}
      <li>Top tags: {{ supp_itch.top_tags | map(attribute=0) | list | join(", ") }}</li>
      {% endif %}
    </ul>
    <p class="caption">itch.io provides no owner/revenue data — coverage counts only.
    Data is one-page scrape, not full catalogue.</p>
    {% else %}
    <p><em>itch.io data not available.</em></p>
    {% endif %}

    <h3>Kongregate</h3>
    {% if supp_kong %}
    <ul>
      <li>Titles found (one page): <strong>{{ supp_kong.count | default('n/a') }}</strong></li>
      <li>Rated titles: <strong>{{ supp_kong.rated_count | default('n/a') }}</strong></li>
      {% if supp_kong.mean_rating_pct is not none %}
      <li>Mean rating (star→%): <strong>{{ supp_kong.mean_rating_pct }}%</strong>
          <em>(low confidence — not comparable to Steam review %)</em></li>
      {% endif %}
      {% if supp_kong.top_tags %}
      <li>Top tags: {{ supp_kong.top_tags | map(attribute=0) | list | join(", ") }}</li>
      {% endif %}
    </ul>
    <p class="caption">Kongregate ratings are 1–5 stars mapped to %; NOT comparable
    to Steam review percentages. Low confidence.</p>
    {% else %}
    <p><em>Kongregate data not available.</em></p>
    {% endif %}

    <h3>Reddit (r/incremental_games)</h3>
    <div class="reddit-note">
      {% if supp_reddit %}
        {{ supp_reddit.note | default('Reddit data status unknown.') }}
        {% if supp_reddit.available and supp_reddit.sentiment %}
        <br>Sentiment counts:
        {% for cat, count in supp_reddit.sentiment.items() %}
          <strong>{{ cat }}</strong>: {{ count }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
        {% endif %}
      {% else %}
        Reddit data unavailable.
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {% if supp_caveats %}
    <h3>Source Caveats</h3>
    <ul>
      {% for c in supp_caveats %}
      <li>{{ c }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

</main>
<footer>
  Idle/Incremental Game Market Analysis &mdash; Steam spine analysis.
  Owner counts: SteamSpy estimates. Mobile not covered.
  <a href="methodology.html">Full methodology &amp; caveats</a>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
